icks very few  viewings information warfare against the  United States the indictment makes much  of pro-trump  and anti-clinton rallies that were  instigated by the Russians but it  doesn't tell us how many people actually  participated in these rallies or whether  they came off at all you know there's  one example of a rally in Texas that was  organized to impose Sharia law and  according to New York Times it attracted  a dozen people there was a counter  protest that according near times was  also organized by the Russians and  attracted a much larger crowd that that  could be two dozen or three dozen people  probably now  we know that that some people in the  real world responded to the agitation  for rallies but we don't know whether  this really amounted to a significant  percentage of voters information warfare  against the United States nor do we know  whether any of this advertising even the  ads that got more attention than the one  with Jesus armwrestling Satan whether  they actually changed anybody's mind or  energized them in any way or got them to  behave in any way different from how  they would have behaved otherwise you  know pro-trump people might turn out for  a pro trump rally and see clinton people  might turn out for anthe Clinton rally  but the fact that they show up does not  necessarily change the outcome of the  election or make the United States and  more acrimonious you know Society let  alone so chaos information warfare  against the United States and the reason  that this sort of hysterical response is  rather alarming is that at bottom we're  talking about speech if you look at the  actual content of these ads in these  tweets it's not qualitatively different  from all the you know homegrown all the  homegrown crap you can routinely see  online this is essentially the same I  mean doesn't mean as good doesn't mean  it's substantive doesn't even mean it's  accurate some of the organs might have  held some water some of them were  completely ridiculous that's true of  American political discourse in general  it's simply the fact that these people  were born in another country that  somehow makes this more alarming than it  would otherwise be I mean if there is a  problem with American democracy in the  sense that people are easily swayed by  emotion this is not a problem that the  Russians created this is a problem that  is much broader than that and to try to  blame you know divisions within the  American political culture on the  Russians seems completely absurd to me  it's much easier you know to blame  foreign invaders for these problems but  the truth is that if voters are making  decisions for stupid reasons that is not  the Russians fault  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]
 

